# Local development (anonymous agent mode, no Convex account needed):
#   CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev
VITE_CONVEX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3211

# Machine runtime (per registered runtime, shown once in the UI). Normally stored
# by `tahcode link` in ~/.tahcode/config.json; these env vars are the CI /
# container fallback (legacy CONVEX_URL / HARNESS_RUNTIME_ID / HARNESS_RUNTIME_TOKEN
# and DALECODE_* are still accepted):
# TAHCODE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210
# TAHCODE_RUNTIME_ID=
# TAHCODE_TOKEN=th_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy env (.env.preview / .env.staging / .env.production)
# Plaintext files are gitignored; only .env.<name>.enc is committed.
# Create with: npm run env:enc -- <preview|staging|production>
# (prompts nothing; reads DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_<NAME> from your shell)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Convex deploy auth (from the Convex dashboard: project settings).
# preview needs a *Preview* deploy key; staging/production a deployment key.
# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY=
# Cloudflare deploy auth (API token + account id)
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Convex Auth signing keys. Generate a pair with:
#   node scripts/generate-auth-keys.mjs >> .env.production
# Keep the PEM on one line (spaces instead of newlines) inside double quotes,
# and the JWKS unquoted or in SINGLE quotes. Do NOT write JWKS="{\"keys\":...}":
# dotenv keeps the backslashes and the deployment serves invalid JSON, which
# breaks every sign-in. CI (scripts/sync-convex-auth-env.mjs) validates both and
# derives the JWKS from the private key if the stored one is unusable.
# JWT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY----- MIIE... -----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# JWKS='{"keys":[{"use":"sig","kty":"RSA","n":"...","e":"AQAB"}]}'
# Google OAuth (optional). Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console with
# the redirect URI https://<deployment>.convex.site/api/auth/callback/google.
# CI syncs both to the Convex deployment when set; alternatively set them once
# in the Convex dashboard (npx convex env set AUTH_GOOGLE_ID ...).
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# NOTE: VITE_CONVEX_URL is injected automatically by `convex deploy
# --cmd-url-env-var-name VITE_CONVEX_URL` during CI; do not store it here.
# Invariant: SITE_URL is the public OAuth return origin. workers.dev is only
# the Worker hostname and must never be written as production SITE_URL.
# CI sets this after deploy (production fail-closes if the host is not
# tahcode.com):
#   production → https://tahcode.com
#   staging    → https://tahcode-staging.gawara.workers.dev
#   preview    → the ephemeral workers.dev / preview-alias URL
# Do not store SITE_URL here.
#
# Preview / staging CI seeds a password user after deploy (Google OAuth is
# not registered on preview hosts). Production is never seeded:
#   test@test.com / test1234  →  /o/preview/settings#connectors
